## Why propagated signatures mattered

The native-only metadata arm reproduced P3's accepted-fold count and symbolic effect exactly, but remained **1.1822× direct**. Thus removing the P3 reference scan/recursive estimator was helpful but not sufficient.

The propagated arm consumed only **29** accepted folds versus **58** for native/P3, yet did much more algebraic pruning. Relative to P3, propagated P4 used **0.1246×** the pair terms and **0.3849×** the multiplications.

The reason is structural: P4 propagates the semantic fact that a subgraph is a two-input truth function of an ordered base pair even when an intermediate local fold would not itself be selected. An ancestor can therefore take one profitable fold that bypasses several lower shells. The signature is metadata, not an eager rewrite.

Across Gate-P, metadata contained **520** propagated-signature nodes and **520** propagated candidate nodes; only demanded nodes reached the lowering selector, which checked **322** binary nodes and accepted 29. Accepted-fold utilization remained **100%**.

Depth trend:

| Gate-P depth | P4 propagated / direct lowering | cases below direct |
|---:|---:|---:|
| 6 | 0.7261× | 6/12 |
| 8 | 0.5365× | 9/12 |
| 10 | 0.4885× | 8/12 |

The synthetic speedup strengthens with Gate-P depth, consistent with the benchmark deliberately containing repeated same-pair structure. This is mechanism evidence, not evidence that ordinary circuits generally have this incidence.

## Construction-inclusive result

| comparison | cases | geometric-mean ratio | bootstrap 95% CI |
|---|---:|---:|---:|
| P4 metadata build + lower / ordinary build + direct lower | 36 | 2.2259 | 1.8913–2.5988 |
| P4 metadata DAG build / ordinary DAG build | 36 | 5.5995 | 4.6396–6.5505 |

Only **3/36** Gate-P cases beat the direct construction-inclusive pipeline. The pooled pipeline result is **2.2259× direct**, so the stronger end-to-end signal does not pass.

The bottleneck has moved decisively into metadata construction: the present object-heavy Python `MetaFactory` takes **5.60×** the ordinary DAG-build time. A post-hoc profile on Gate-P 10:2 localized most construction cost to `MetaFactory._make` and `_candidate_from_children`, not to the now-fast propagated ANF lowering.

**Predeclared Gate-P construction-inclusive speed signal: NO PASS.**

