## Bottom line

P4 separates two questions that were conflated in P3. **Once the tiny two-support signature is already present, profitable propagated folding can beat direct sparse ANF substantially on the fold-rich Gate-P mechanism benchmark.** The unresolved engineering problem is no longer the lowering algorithm; it is making signature/fanout/estimate propagation cheap enough during DAG construction.
